    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in HD:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " a VMAT-2 inhibitor (tetrabenazine, deutetrabenazine) = typical first-line symptomatic tx of chorea; doses ↑ stepwise as tolerated; avoid w depression (↑worsening depression and suicidality);"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tetrabenazine (Xenazine) dose, chorea of Huntington's disease:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Start 12.5 mg/day in the morning; after 1 wk, 25 mg/day as 12.5 mg twice a day; then titrate slowly at weekly intervals by 12.5 mg daily to a tolerated dose that ↓chorea. Doses >50 mg/day require CYP2D6 genotyping (poor vs extensive metabolizer). Max daily dose: PMs 50 mg (max single 25 mg); EMs/IMs 100 mg (max single 37.5 mg)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tetrabenazine (Xenazine) boxed warning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ↑ risk of depression and suicidal thoughts & behavior (suicidality) in pts w Huntington's disease; balance against the clinical need to control chorea. pts actively suicidal, or depression untreated or inadequately treated."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tetrabenazine (Xenazine) CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " hepatic impairment. CI: MAOIs or reserpine."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tetrabenazine (Xenazine) key warnings:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " NMS: discontinue XENAZINE if it occurs. Akathisia: reduce dose; some pts require discontinuation. Parkinsonism: consider dose reduction; in some pts discontinuation may be necessary. Causes a small ↑ in QTc (~8 msec)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tetrabenazine (Xenazine) interactions:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Strong CYP2D6 inhibitors: daily dose ≤50 mg, max single ≤25 mg. Neuroleptics may ↑ risk of parkinsonism, NMS, and akathisia."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
